{"parentUuid":"3d5baa31-e96e-49b2-beb2-898aa921b734","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5070327a1e24b779","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01MvWr3uDkGZcgGH8V7oaVM2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Jo4DTVnuuTh6pynAgsorJX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git log --grep \"P1 #9\" --pretty=format:\"%H%n%s%n%b%n---\" 2>&1 | head -120","description":"Get full P1 #9 commit messages"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7937,"cache_read_input_tokens":20408,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7937,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CasSFdB8HbLCGMCyGMKC8","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"aa7d2dd6-e723-4605-b3a6-d36402f54c2a","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:04:02.950Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"aa7d2dd6-e723-4605-b3a6-d36402f54c2a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a8f1a005-6197-4ac8-b6c3-3f7619cec3c7","agentId":"a5070327a1e24b779","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jo4DTVnuuTh6pynAgsorJX","type":"tool_result","content":"94351d54b95840f61ddd01def2db79915c185f69\nP1 #9 hint 2 stage 3: caller fallback ladder for overload separation\nWhen EXACT_BINDING_USE_OVERLOAD_SEPARATION is on AND the first-pass\nbinding solve returns INFEASIBLE AND nogoods were actually injected,\nLBBDController now retries the binding once with the env temporarily\nforced off:\n\n- FEASIBLE  -> the first INFEASIBLE was a spurious result of the\n               heuristic high+low colocation forbidding (player\n               consensus, not a SAT invariant); swap to retry model\n               and continue normally\n- INFEASIBLE -> genuine infeasibility, fall through to the existing\n               whole-layout-nogood handler (binding_summary still\n               carries first-pass overload_*  fields)\n- TIMEOUT    -> env-off status genuinely unknown; return UNKNOWN\n               rather than certifying INFEASIBLE on a heuristic\n               proof — soundness over throughput\n\nNew helper LBBDController._retry_binding_without_overload_separation\nsaves/restores os.environ in try/finally so a solver exception still\nleaves the env clean for subsequent iterations.\n\nThis finally closes the env-on safety gap noted in stage 2 commit\n1ba7ca2 (\"Stage 3 NOT YET WIRED UP — until stage 3 lands, leave env\nunset to avoid INFEASIBLE risk\"). With stage 3 in, enabling the env\nin production becomes safe (worst case = one wasted retry per\nspurious-INFEASIBLE wave).\n\nVerified:\n- 13 test_binding tests pass (10 prior + 3 new)\n- 2044 full pytest pass, 60 skipped (no regression vs 2035 baseline,\n  delta covers 3 new + other in-tree additions)\n- preflight gate 8/8\n\nThe 3 new tests cover the helper in isolation:\n1. env=1 going in -> '' during build -> '1' restored after\n2. env unset going in -> '' during build -> popped after\n3. env restored even when solve raises (try/finally contract)\n\nIntegration of the wiring (the second 'if INFEASIBLE' guard +\nTIMEOUT->UNKNOWN branch) is verified by diff review; constructing a\nfixture that synthesizes a real spurious-INFEASIBLE on the project\ndata is stage 5 territory and not in scope here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n22af98af2172128d09abad2c3fea6ba7bb45157c\nP1 #9 hint 2 stage 4: unit tests for overload separation env-gated logic\nTwo tests verify the env-gated wiring of stage 2:\n\n1. test_binding_model_overload_separation_default_off:\n   - explicitly delenv EXACT_BINDING_USE_OVERLOAD_SEPARATION\n   - assert conflict_summary[\"overload_separation_enabled\"] is False\n   - assert overload_nogoods_added == 0\n\n2. test_binding_model_overload_separation_when_enabled_records_summary:\n   - setenv EXACT_BINDING_USE_OVERLOAD_SEPARATION=1\n   - build() must succeed (no infeasibility cascade on this single\n     wireless_sink fixture)\n   - assert overload_separation_enabled is True\n   - overload_nogoods_added >= 0 (concrete count depends on real\n     project classification — not asserted, just non-negative)\n\nThese cover the wiring layer; semantic verification on real wave\ndata is stage 5 (deferred — requires campaign state which isn't\nsynced from Windows yet).\n\nVerified:\n- test_binding: 10 passed (was 8 + 2 new)\n- full pytest: 2035 passed, 0 failed, 60 skipped (+2 from baseline 2033)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n1ba7ca2f92f7d46e7a5721c79abda0f559db644a\nP1 #9 hint 2 stage 2: storage-box overload nogood (env-gated default off)\nWires up the commodity classification helper (commit 281aba9 stage 1)\ninto BindingSubproblem.build():\n\n- New helper _load_overload_classification(): lazy-reads\n  canonical_rules.json, computes throughput over self.instances_by_id\n  via compute_commodity_throughput(), classifies each commodity as\n  high_prod_low_demand / low_prod_high_demand / balanced\n  (threshold_ratio=0.1)\n- New method _add_storage_box_overload_nogoods(): for every\n  protocol_storage_box instance (operation_type=wireless_sink) and\n  every (c_high, c_low) pair, adds CP-SAT clause AddBoolOr([h.Not(),\n  l.Not()]) on every input-slot literal pair — forbids the player-\n  consensus \"high+low pair in same box causes throughput stall\"\n  configuration\n\nActivation via env EXACT_BINDING_USE_OVERLOAD_SEPARATION ∈ {1,true,yes,on}.\nDefault unset → no behavior change → existing pytest baseline preserved.\n\nVerified:\n- conflict_summary now reports overload_separation_enabled and\n  overload_nogoods_added\n- test_binding: 8 passed\n- full pytest: 2033 passed, 0 failed, 60 skipped (no regression)\n\nStage 3 (caller-side fallback ladder) NOT YET WIRED UP — when env is\non and binding goes INFEASIBLE due to forced high+low colocation,\ncaller (outer_search / benders_loop) must detect and retry with env\nunset. Until stage 3 lands, leave env unset to avoid INFEASIBLE\nrisk; the helpers and method exist for shadow-mode A/B testing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n281aba99e6e80882c5eb0d473df050abdf968aae\nP1 #9 hint 2 stage 1: commodity throughput helper (pure, no model side effect)\nStandalone module computing per-commodity production_rate /\nconsumption_rate / net_flow from canonical_rules.json (recipes) and\nmandatory_exact_instances.json (operation_type counts).\n\nPlus classify_commodity_flow() bucketing each commodity into\nhigh_prod_low_demand / low_prod_high_demand / balanced based on\nconfigurable threshold_ratio (default ±10% of max(prod,cons)).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e6e96bfb-9cfd-4226-b6a9-6751f39e0dab","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:04:02.967Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aa7d2dd6-e723-4605-b3a6-d36402f54c2a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
